WEBVTT

00:00:00.326 --> 00:00:05.478
This is the vNAAATS handoff helper. A helping hand, not a hand on the controls.

00:00:06.566 --> 00:00:20.640
The Handoff Helper is not a feature to take control away from you. It is a helping hand, a reminder to hand off, especially in busy periods, when entry traffic is loading into the NAT region, and it is easy for one aircraft to slip past its boundary.

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:26.758
When an aircraft you are tracking nears its boundary, the handoff button flashes yellow in the toolbar.

00:00:27.046 --> 00:00:27.974
short chime.

00:00:28.326 --> 00:00:32.582
Click it to read the message. If you prefer quiet, the sound can be switched off.

00:00:33.926 --> 00:00:41.542
The card shows which aircraft it is, how far it is from the boundary, and which sector is next. Choose a controller who is online and press transfer.

00:00:41.894 --> 00:00:43.750
EuroScope does the transfer for you.

00:00:45.446 --> 00:00:49.638
The pilot is on CPDLC. They are sent the contact message for you.

00:00:50.246 --> 00:00:52.678
off once they answer Wilco or Roger.

00:00:54.022 --> 00:00:55.974
Nobody is online to take the aircraft.

00:00:56.262 --> 00:00:59.750
The card waits until it is at the boundary, then offers handoff to Unica.

00:01:00.422 --> 00:01:03.782
The pilot is told to monitor 122 decimal 800.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:10.470
If the pilot is not on CPDLC, tell them by voice or text.

00:01:11.686 --> 00:01:27.296
If you would like even more help, there is Auto Handoff. It is off by default. For aircraft you track that are on CPDLC, it sends the transfer for you at the distance you choose from 10 to 50 nautical miles when a controller is online to take it. With nobody online, it sends the UNICOM message at the boundary.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:32.038
Each action is tried once, and if it fails, the card comes up so you can do it by hand.

00:01:33.382 --> 00:01:38.502
Between Shanwick and Gander, a flight crossing 30 West is handed to the other oceanic center.

00:01:38.854 --> 00:01:41.606
when a combined NAT FSS position is online.

00:01:41.926 --> 00:01:42.854
There is no problem

00:01:43.494 --> 00:01:46.278
The controller works both areas on one frequency.

00:01:47.462 --> 00:02:01.568
To sum up, the reminder flashes and chimes. Transfer or hand off to Unicom in one click. Switch on auto handoff if you want it done for you. It is there to help in busy entry periods into the NAT region, so no aircraft is missed and you always stay in-

